-- chem/witness.cub — the one producer of witnesses: Bareiss's fraction-free elimination returning its congruence
-- witness as integers. For a symmetric integer matrix N with leading minors D_1 … D_n nonzero, run the elimination
-- of chem/inertia.cub (in-rows, every division exact) on the augmented rows [N | 1]. After k − 1 steps the k-th row
-- begins with the pivot D_k, and its last n entries are the minors of the first k rows of [N | 1] on the columns
-- 1 … k − 1 and n + j: the vector w_k = D_k·N_k⁻¹e_k (the k-th column of the adjugate of the leading k × k block,
-- zeros after position k, D_{k−1} at position k). Since N w_k has zeros at positions 1 … k − 1 and D_k at k, and w_j
-- for j < k has zeros from position j + 1 on, w_jᵀ N w_k = 0 for j < k and w_kᵀ N w_k = D_k·D_{k−1}: a diagonalizing
-- witness with integer entries bounded by the minors of N, at the cost of the elimination itself (n³ updates of
-- numbers of at most n·b bits for b-bit entries), where the rational Gram–Schmidt of chem/hecert.cub pays for
-- denominators and gcds. The producer is untrusted: nothing about it is proved or needed. The trusted step is
-- chem/zring.cub's `inertia-cert` on its output, whose count is the form's inertia for every passing witness
-- (`inertia-cert-sound`). A bracket of a level of a pencil is then three such counts, at ends found by any search.
import "hecert.hypercubical"

